DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin((ln(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin(((x*3)^3))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[2, 7] U ((({-5, -4, 2} U [2, 7])))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-5, -4, 2} U [2, 7] U [2, 7]");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("([2, 7]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-5, -4, 2} U [2, 7]))) U {-5, -4, 2}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-8, 2, 4} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, 2, 4}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, 2, 4})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{8, 9} U ({8, 9}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {8, 9}) U {8, 9} U {-8, 2, 4}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({8, 9} U {-8, 2, 4}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, 2, 4}) U {-8, 2, 4}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`5*8+14`] is equal to [_____]{54}
---

What is the value of [`12+11+5/6`]? [_____]{answer=>23.8333333333,width=>4}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{8, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, 2, 4\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup (A) \cap A \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A \cup B) \cap B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-5, -4, 2\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup (((A \cup B))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(B) \cap ((A \cup B)) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, -7, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, 6, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, -7, 9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 6, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -7, 9>") . Compute("<-10, 6, -7>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 6, -7>") x Compute("<1, -7, 9>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 2, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 10, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, 10, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 2, 7>") x Compute("<-5, 10, -5>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -5>") . Compute("<2, 10, -8>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
